DESIGN GOAL

I wanted to give the player fun dialogue options with the villagers. I decided to use scripted dialogue to achieve a more intuitive and straightforward experience.

SHORT REFLECTION:

I decided to use scripted dialogue techniques.
I let the characters stick to their roles while adding some more to it. There is now a new role: the lightkeeper, who sets the torches up and keeps in mind which torches they've lit. The player
can ask NPCs what lanterns are lit and if they can't see them, they won't know. The lightkeeper, however, knows if a lantern is lit or not. Additionally, I added dialogue options that only certain NPCs have
that connect to other NPCs ' dialogue options, creating a mini quest for the player. Additionally, there is a dialogue option that uses open-ended player messages instead of scripted numbered messages.

AI DISCLOSURE:

I used Claude Code in this agent. It helped modify code and implement ideas. It made the project much easier to complete and allowed me to use much more complex techniques.
